			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Extend extension cache lifetime and refine SCM updates\n\nIncrease the maximum cache age for extension descriptors from 10 minutes to 24 hours. The previous window was too tight for local development workflows where the binary and cache are co-located; since builds regenerate the cache, a longer duration prevents unnecessary rescans without staleness risks.\n\nEnhance the `FileWriteNative` handler to suppress false-positive warnings when the Cocoon process is not yet connected during `FileWrite` operations. This prevents noise in the `vfs` log when saving files before the extension host is fully ready.\n\nAlign `UpdateScmGroup` logic to emit `scmId` alongside `providerId` in the payload to `sky://scm/updateGroup`. This ensures the Sky frontend can correctly resolve the SCM shim. Remove the fallback logic that attempted to invoke `UpdateSourceControlGroup` traits, as direct event emission is the reliable path.\n\nAdditionally, add `DebugServer`, `DebugServerPortMountain`, and `DebugServerPortCocoon` to the environment variable whitelist in `CocoonManagement` to support future debugging configurations.",
			"SHA": "fc1e6daf52356219f8c954cc53b698a688432d94"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T05:33:57Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1739,
				2
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Prevent Tauri build failure on missing Sky manifest\n\nThe Tauri build process fails when running `cargo build` directly because it validates `extensions.manifest.json` referenced in `bundle.resources`, which is normally generated by the Sky frontend build. Update `build.rs` to create a stub file (`[]`) at the expected path if missing, ensuring the build succeeds without a prior Sky build while retaining the live scan fallback in `LoadFromCache.rs`.\n\nAdditionally, disable `beforeBundleCommand` in `tauri.conf.json` to prevent redundant or conflicting manifest generation steps during the Tauri build phase, relying instead on the explicit manifest creation in `build.rs` and the existing Sky build pipeline.",
			"SHA": "3473a81e819f0b8a80fc02084589693a1fe0d85d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T04:26:15Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1739,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Mountain): Add lint allowances to build script for generated bindings\n\nPreserve build stability by re-allowing standard naming and usage lints (`non_snake_case`, `dead_code`, etc.) within `build.rs`. This compensates for the recent global removal of `#![allow(non_snake_case)]` across the source tree, which inadvertently flagged warnings in build scripts consuming auto-generated protocol bindings or external definitions.\n\nThe change ensures the build process remains clean while the main application source maintains strict PascalCase compliance and active linting. This aligns with the pattern in `Source/Vine/Generated/mod.rs` where specific allowances are retained for non-manual code.",
			"SHA": "f520c6044f6940106f177b01327ed613e11f7846"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T04:21:08Z",
			"File": [
				"⡟⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1739,
				245
			],
			"Message": "style(Mountain): Remove pervasive leading empty lines after module doc comments\n\nStrip the redundant single empty line immediately following `//! ...` module doc comments across over 400 files in the Mountain backend. This affects Air integration, Binary entry points, Command handlers, Environment providers, ExtensionManagement, and the full IPC layer (WindServiceHandlers, RPC/CocoonService, Track, Vine).\n\nThe change enforces a tighter file header style where documentation blocks are directly followed by the first code declaration or `use` statement, eliminating stylistic noise while preserving all logic and API contracts. `Source/Library.rs` retain necessary global allowances for generated code, while the rest of the source tree now adheres to a uniform header structure.\n\nRefs #CLAUDE.md",
			"SHA": "2a4878c8f2eebf57350b1ee6725633c2d3199a53"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T04:21:00Z",
			"File": [
				"⡿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1739,
				300
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Remove pervasive dead_code and unused_imports allowances\n\nStrip `#![allow(dead_code, unused_imports, unused_variables)]` and related lint suppressions from over 200 files across the Mountain backend. This cleanup spans the Air integration, ApplicationState, Binary entry points, ExtensionManagement, IPC layers (WindServiceHandlers, Vine, TauriIPC, SecureChannel), RPC services (Cocoon, Echo, Workspace), Telemetry, Track, and Update modules.\n\nRemove redundant `#[allow(dead_code)]` and `#[allow(unused_imports)]` attributes from structs, constants, traits, functions, and module-level declarations. Also normalize file headers by removing leading empty lines and unused import groups to align with the project-wide PascalCase and strict linting standards.\n\nEnsure `Source/Library.rs` retains only necessary global allowances for generated code and external bindings, while `Source/Binary/Main/Entry.rs` and build scripts are updated to reflect the new strict lint policy. This change eliminates style noise from reviews and ensures future code additions adhere to the required naming and usage conventions.\n\nRefs #CLAUDE.md",
			"SHA": "350d161450f66626001a72885bfde33237ae9dfd"
		}
	],
